    <item>
      <title>Honest Opinions on Linux Distros</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/distros-opinion/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Mar 2026 10:30:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/distros-opinion/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;my-rating-of-linux-distros&#34;&gt;My rating of Linux distros&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;1-opensuse-tumbleweed&#34;&gt;1. OpenSUSE Tumbleweed&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This one is honestly by far the best Linux distro I think you can use.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pros:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;✅ It&amp;rsquo;s incredibly stable. Before they publish any update, they test the software before publishing it. So it&amp;rsquo;s far more stable than other rolling-release distros (like Arch).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;✅ It&amp;rsquo;s rolling-release, as I said, as soon as new software comes, they test it and release it. So you dont have to wait a long time to enjoy a new KDE / other fresh software.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Cool Linux tools</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/documents/cool-commands/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 15:30:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/documents/cool-commands/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;-a-terminal-based-file-manager&#34;&gt;&amp;gt; A terminal based file manager&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;yazi&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;yazi&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;-a-set-of-eyes-on-your-screen-that-follow-your-cursor-if-the-window-is-running-through-xwayland-good-way-to-check-wayland-compatibility&#34;&gt;&amp;gt; A set of eyes on your screen that follow your cursor if the window is running through XWayland. Good way to check Wayland compatibility.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;xeyes&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;xeyes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;xorg-xeyes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;-terminal-that-has-built-in-image-compatibility-and-doesnt-require-weird-commands-for-using-ssh-and-stuff-like-kitty-does&#34;&gt;&amp;gt; Terminal that has built in image compatibility, and doesnt require weird commands for using ssh and stuff like kitty does.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;foot&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;foot&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;-tool-for-displaying-images-in-a-terminal-goes-well-with-foot&#34;&gt;&amp;gt; Tool for displaying images in a terminal (goes well with &lt;code&gt;foot&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;chafa &amp;lt;image_file&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;chafa&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Linux Basics</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/documents/linux-basics/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 20:30:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/documents/linux-basics/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;exam-example&#34;&gt;Exam example&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;part-1-basic-knowledge&#34;&gt;Part 1: Basic knowledge&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;print-all-files-in-a-directory-including-hidden-files-permissions-group-and-user-owners&#34;&gt;Print all files in a directory, including hidden files, permissions, group and user owners&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ls -la /path/to/directory&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;print-first-15-lines-of-a-file&#34;&gt;Print first 15 lines of a file&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;head -n &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;15&lt;/span&gt; /path/to/file&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;get-free-memory&#34;&gt;Get free memory&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;free -h&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;show-disk-block-devices&#34;&gt;Show disk block devices&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;lsblk&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;show-all-processes-running-under-root&#34;&gt;Show all processes running under root&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;simple way (not 100% correct):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ps aux | grep root&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;more correct way:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ps -U root -u root&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;what-is-grub-and-what-is-it-for&#34;&gt;What is GRUB and what is it for?&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;GRUB is a Linux bootloader. It&amp;rsquo;s responsible for loading the kernel, initializing the system and it provides a menu to select an operating system to boot.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Fix Distrobox xdg-open</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/snippets/distrobox-xdg-open/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 15:30:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/snippets/distrobox-xdg-open/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 1. Clean broken paths to prevent &amp;#34;command not found&amp;#34; errors&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/xdg-open&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/distrobox-host-exec&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 2. Create the bridge in /usr/local/bin (High Priority Location)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo tee /usr/local/bin/xdg-open &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt; &amp;#39;EOF&amp;#39;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;#!/usr/bin/python3&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;import sys, dbus, os&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;# Ensure the Host D-Bus is found&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;os.environ[&amp;#34;DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS&amp;#34;] = f&amp;#34;unix:path=/run/user/{os.getuid()}/bus&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;try:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    url = sys.argv[1]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    bus = dbus.SessionBus()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    obj = bus.get_object(&amp;#34;org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;/org/freedesktop/portal/desktop&amp;#34;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    iface = dbus.Interface(obj, &amp;#34;org.freedesktop.portal.OpenURI&amp;#34;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    iface.OpenURI(&amp;#34;&amp;#34;, url, {})&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;except Exception:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;    pass&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;EOF&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 3. Set execution permissions&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo chmod &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;755&lt;/span&gt; /usr/local/bin/xdg-open&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 4. Create Distrobox integration links&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo ln -sf /usr/local/bin/xdg-open /usr/local/bin/distrobox-host-exec&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 5. FIX FOR ICONS: Global Variable in /etc/environment&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# This ensures that GUI apps (like Antigravity) see the bridge even when opened via the menu&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo sh -c &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;echo &amp;#39;BROWSER=\&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin/xdg-open\&amp;#34;&amp;#39; &amp;gt;&amp;gt; /etc/environment&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# 6. Update PATH for the current terminal session (Bash/Fish/Zsh)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;export PATH&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin:&lt;/span&gt;$PATH&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;export BROWSER&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin/xdg-open&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;hash -r 2&amp;gt;/dev/null &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; true&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;✅ Setup Finished! Testing...&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;xdg-open https://www.google.com&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# CREDIT: https://github.com/89luca89/distrobox/issues/1984&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>My Story With ThinkPads</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/thinkpad-story/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 24 Jan 2026 21:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/thinkpad-story/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;how-i-got-into-thinkpads&#34;&gt;How I Got Into Thinkpads&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been a Linux user for quite some time now, and it&amp;rsquo;s impossible to be a Linux die-hard without encountering ThinkPads. My journey with ThinkPads began several years ago when I got my first one, a ThinkPad T480.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;my-thinkpad-t480&#34;&gt;My ThinkPad T480&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is where my ThinkPad adventure began. The T480 is an excellent laptop, in fact, I&amp;rsquo;m writing this part on it right now!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s built like a tank, but not a big tank, a relatively slim, portable tank (compared to the T420).&#xA;And it has a fantastic keyboard, as all older ThinkPads do.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Linux Distro Chooser</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/apps/distro-chooser/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 24 Jan 2026 01:20:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/apps/distro-chooser/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;decide-on-the-perfect-linux-distro-for-you&#34;&gt;Decide on the perfect Linux distro for you!&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is a simple Linux Distro Chooser tool that I created to help people find the perfect Linux distribution for&#xA;their needs. It is based on my personal experience and recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;try-it-out&#34;&gt;Try it out!&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;script&#xA;  defer&#xA;  src=&#34;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/alpinejs@3.x.x/dist/cdn.min.js&#34;&#xA;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/css/minigame-styles.css?v=1773943029&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/js/distro-chooser.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;box-mg&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div x-data=&#34;distroChooser()&#34; class=&#34;distro-widget&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div x-show=&#34;step === 0&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;h3&gt;Find the perfect Linux distribution for you!&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;&#xA;        Answer a few simple questions and get an answer, that&#39;s based on my&#xA;        experience and reccomendation.&#xA;      &lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
  </channel>
</rss>
